 "measured": {
  "chart": {
   "ideal": "Greedy in both axes. With no height proposed (in a ScrollView) a Chart is 100 tall; with no frame in a padded VStack it takes all the height (746).",
   "plotFrame": "Chart frame less the trailing y axis column and the bottom x axis row, and less the legend row when there is one. Hidden axes give the whole frame to the plot.",
   "yAxisColumn": "ceil(widest label width) + 4: '10,000' (35.67 wide) gives 40, '20,000' (37.33) 42, '80' and '40' (14.33) 19, '30' (14.0) 18, '8' and '6' (7.33) 12. Labels are leading aligned 4 after the plot's trailing edge, each centred vertically on its tick (the top one reaches 6.67 above the chart's frame).",
   "xAxisRow": "18 = ceil(4 + 13.33): label boxes 4 below the plot. Categorical labels are centred in their band; numeric and date labels start 4 after their grid line, and the label at the domain's upper end is left out ('30' at 0...30, '10,000' on the horizontal chart).",
   "labelFont": ".caption2 (11 pt, line 13.33), secondaryLabel: rgb(138,138,142) on white, rgb(141,141,147) on black.",
   "gridLines": "0.5 pt in tertiaryLabel (60,60,67 at 0.3; core pixel 197,197,199 on white, about 61 on black). Lines across (horizontal) are solid, from the plot's leading to trailing edge; lines down (vertical) are dashed 2 on 2 starting at the plot top, and run on through the x axis row. Vertical bars: horizontal lines at each y tick, dashed lines at every band edge including both ends. Horizontal bars: solid lines at band edges, dashed at x ticks. Numeric x: dashed at each tick. Dates: dashed at the plot's edges and each labelled day.",
   "ticks": "Steps from 1, 2, 5 x 10^k, plus 2.5 x 10^k for k >= 1, the smallest giving at most 4 intervals from floor(min/step) to ceil(max/step), the domain always holding 0 and widened to those multiples. Tops seen: 0.3->0.3 (0.1), 0.8->0.8 (0.2), 1->1 (0.5), 3->3 (1), 4.5->6 (2), 5->6 (2), 8->8 (2), 9->10 (5), 12->15 (5), 17->20 (5), 21->30 (10), 23->30 (10), 33->40 (10), 40->40 (10), 47->60 (20), 80->80 (20), 95->100 (25), 130->150 (50), 250->300 (100), 1800->2000 (500), 8800->10000 (2500); -3..7 -> -5..10 (5), -40..15 -> -40..20 (20). The number of ticks doesn't change with the plot's height (222 or 728). chartYScale(domain: 0...20000) keeps that domain and ticks it by 5000.",
   "tickLabels": "Grouped thousands: 10,000, 7,500, 2,500; fractions as written: 0.5, 0.2.",
   "dates": "unit: .day: a band per day from the first to the last, labels 'MMM d' starting 4 after the band's leading edge: every day for 3 days, every second day from the first for 7, and on Sundays (the week's first day in en_US) for 14 and 30. With no unit: dates are plotted on a continuous time axis, not in bands: hourly points from 9:00 to 14:00 run edge to edge of the plot with ticks each hour labelled '9 AM'; bars over seven days at noon are narrow (about 8 pt) and centred on the instant, with ticks at every second midnight ('Jun 17'); bars on the first of six months are as narrow, with ticks every second month ('Jan', 'Mar', 'May'). The first and last bars reach past the plot's edges.",
   "palette": "foregroundStyle(by:) series in first-seen order take blue, green, orange, purple, red, teal, yellow, then repeat. Light: (0,136,255) (52,199,89) (255,141,40) (203,48,224) (255,56,60) (0,195,208) (255,204,0). Dark: (0,145,255) (48,209,88) (255,146,48) (219,52,242) (255,66,69) (0,210,224) (255,214,0). An unstyled mark is the accent, the palette's first.",
   "legend": "Below the chart, leading: 4 below the x axis row, a row 13.33 tall. Each entry an 8 pt circle, the series name 5 after it in .caption2 secondaryLabel, entries 8 apart, in first-seen order. The legend takes 17.33 from the plot. chartLegend(.hidden) gives it back.",
   "bars": "0.7 of the band, centred. Rounded 2 pt at the end away from zero only (a stack's outer end; a negative bar's bottom). Stacks from zero in the order the data gives at each x, not by series: with Feb written Juice, Tea, Coffee, Juice is at the bottom and Coffee on top (stack-order). position(by:) splits the 0.7 band into one sub-band per series and draws each bar 0.7 of its sub-band, centred. Horizontal bars (numeric x, categorical y): the band's label sits inside the plot, 4 from the leading edge and 4 below the band's top, and the bar takes 0.7 of the band below it (band less 17.33), centred there; no y axis column.",
   "line": "LineMark 2 pt, round joins, accent; PointMark an 8 pt disc; both at the band's centre for categorical x.",
   "area": "AreaMark filled solid in the accent from zero to the values, band centre to band centre.",
   "rule": "RuleMark(y:) or (x:) a 2 pt line in the accent across the whole plot.",
   "sector": "SectorMark: a pie centred in the plot, radius half the plot's shorter side (111.33 in a 370 x 222.67 plot), starting at 12 o'clock and going clockwise in data order. innerRadius .ratio(0.6) leaves a hole of 0.6 of the radius. angularInset 1.5 leaves a gap 3 pt wide with parallel sides between sectors. Charts with only sectors have no axes or grid. Overlay annotations sit at the sector's middle angle, 0.618 of the way from the inner to the outer radius.",
   "annotation": "position .top: the content's bottom 4 above the bar's top, centred on the band; .overlay: centred on the mark. Content is drawn as written (black .caption here). A RuleMark's .top annotation: for RuleMark(y:) the content's bottom 4 above the line, centred on the plot; for RuleMark(x:) 4 above the plot's top, centred on the rule (rule-annotation). A SectorMark's .top annotation draws nothing (sector-top).",
   "hidden": "chartXAxis(.hidden) and chartYAxis(.hidden) remove the labels, ticks and grid lines; the plot takes the frame.",
   "domain": "chartXScale(domain:) with an array of categories on a category x axis gives one band per category in the domain's order, the ones with no data left empty (Mon to Sun over Mon to Fri data: 7 bands of 47.14). With a closed range of dates on a day axis, the bands run over the domain's days, labelled every second day from its first (xscale-date: Jun 13 to Jun 23, 11 days).",
   "gradient": "A gradient foregroundStyle on a LineMark runs across the line itself, its first stop at the first point and its last at the last (gradient: (255,57,62), the red itself, at Mon's point, not a blend); on a RuleMark across the rule, which is the whole plot.",
   "empty": "A Chart over empty data draws nothing at all: no axes, grid or frame, only the space it takes (empty)."
  }
